            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for to push back, then the Gujarati for at long last."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ઝંઝટ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઝંઝટ — jhanjhaṭ — \"a hassle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "જો ટ્રેન મોડી હશે તો ઘણી ઝંઝટ થશે. jo ṭren moḍī haśe to ghaṇī jhanjhaṭ thaśe. If the train is late, there will be a lot of hassle."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઝંઝટ (jhanjhaṭ) sounds like what it means, a tangle of small troubles. CDIAL lists Old Gujarati jhaṁjha, \"a quarrel\", and Gujarati jhā̃jh, \"rage\", under Sanskrit jhañjhā, \"the noise of rain\" (CDIAL 5326); it does not list this word, so its history is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
